course: dictionary
lesson: 15612
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and a dictionary lists them as 1), 2), 3). Read the sentence to find the right one. «The doctor pointed to the tarsus on the skeleton diagram.» The science clue, skeleton, tells you tarsus means the small bones of the ankle.
explain: Tarsus can also name a part of a bird's or insect's leg, near the foot. «The bird stood on its thin, yellow tarsus.» Here the bird is the clue, so the word means a body part of the leg, not a bone in a person's ankle. Ask yourself what the sentence is about.
explain: A name can be a word too. «Saint Paul came from Tarsus, an old city.» Tarsus with a capital T, and the words city and came, show it is a place. Capital letters are a clue, but always check the other words before you decide.
fact: Tarsus means the group of small bones in the ankle and upper foot.
fact: In birds and insects, the tarsus is a part of the leg near the foot.
fact: Tarsus is also the name of an old city, now in Turkey.
fact: The plural of tarsus is tarsi.
fact: Metatarsals are the foot bones and phalanges are the toe bones, so in a skeleton lesson the tarsus is the ankle group that comes between the leg and the foot.
exercise: «The doctor pointed to the tarsus on the skeleton diagram.» What does tarsus mean here? | A part of a fish's fin | A pointed tool for cutting paper | The name of a city in Turkey | *The small bones of the ankle and upper foot
exercise: «The bird stood on its thin, yellow tarsus.» What is the tarsus in this sentence? | *A part of the leg near the foot | A bone in a person's ankle | A feather on the wing | A small nest in a tree
exercise: Saint Paul came from «Tarsus», an old city. Is Tarsus a body part or a place? | A body part | An insect's wing | A bird | *A place
test: The plural of tarsus is tarsi. Which word is the plural? | *tarsi | tarsa | tarsii | tarsuses
test: In a Bible lesson, «Saul of Tarsus» most likely means Saul came from which kind of word? | A kind of bone in the foot | *A place name | A fish's fin | A bird's leg
exam: «The tarsus is the group of small bones in the ankle.» What does tarsus mean? | *The small bones of the ankle and upper foot | A bird's song | A city in Turkey | A type of ankle sock
